      <!-- Introduction -->
      <p>
        Selling on Amazon India provides merchants with unmatched access to hundreds of millions of high-intent shoppers, Prime subscribers, and nationwide delivery reach. However, translating high sales volume into sustainable business wealth requires complete clarity on Amazon’s complex fee structure. Without using a dedicated <strong>amazon profit calculator</strong>, many sellers miscalculate deductions and inadvertently price their listings at an operational loss. Integrating our <a href="/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">all-in-one seller profit calculator</a> into your daily catalog workflow ensures every SKU remains profitable before fulfillment begins.
      </p>

      <p>
        Whether you fulfill orders via Easy Ship, Fulfilled by Amazon (FBA), or Self-Ship (FBM), our real-time <strong>amazon revenue calculator india</strong> simulates the exact deduction waterfall applied to every customer transaction. By understanding how an <strong>amazon seller calculator</strong> computes referral fees, closing slabs, courier logistics, and statutory taxes, you can set winning prices using an intuitive <a href="/selling-price-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">selling price calculator</a> that protects your margins while staying competitive in search rankings.
      </p>

      <!-- H3: Complete Breakdown of Amazon India Fees -->
      <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 pt-2 border-t border-neutral-100">
        How the Amazon Calculator Deducts Selling Fees: The 2026 Slabs
      </h3>
      <p>
        When an order is placed on Amazon India, the gross selling price undergoes a sequential series of deductions before the net payout is disbursed to your registered bank account. Here is the exact fee architecture incorporated into our <strong>amazon revenue calculator</strong>:
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-neutral-600">
        <li>
          <strong>1. Category Referral Fee (3% to 15%):</strong> Amazon charges a percentage of the total item selling price as a platform facilitation commission. For example, consumer electronics and computing peripherals typically carry 4.5% to 7.5% referral fees, home &amp; kitchen products incur 8% to 10.5%, and fashion apparel carries 12% to 13.5%. These rates are tied to the retail selling price and category taxonomy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>2. Dynamic Closing Fee Slabs:</strong> A fixed per-unit fee charged on all delivered products based on total sales price thresholds. Under Amazon India’s standard Easy Ship schedule, the tiers are:
          <ul class="list-circle pl-5 mt-1 space-y-1 text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <li>₹1 to ₹250: ₹5 closing fee</li>
            <li>₹251 to ₹500: ₹11 closing fee</li>
            <li>₹501 to ₹1,000: ₹25 closing fee</li>
            <li>₹1,001 to ₹2,000: ₹35 closing fee</li>
            <li>₹2,001 and above: ₹42 to ₹50 closing fee</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>3. Easy Ship Weight Handling Fee:</strong> Based on the chargeable weight of your package (actual weight vs volumetric weight). Use our <a href="/shipping-cost-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">e-commerce shipping cost calculator</a> to estimate courier rates across local, regional, and national transit zones.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>4. 18% GST on Seller Fees:</strong> The Government of India requires Amazon to collect 18% Goods and Services Tax on the sum of all service fees (referral commission + closing fee + courier shipping). You can verify your tax incidence with our <a href="/gst-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">GST calculator online</a>, and registered GST sellers can reclaim this 100% as Input Tax Credit using our <a href="/input-tax-credit-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">Input Tax Credit (ITC) calculator</a> to offset sales tax liability.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>5. Regulatory Withholdings (TCS &amp; TDS):</strong> 0.5% Tax Collected at Source under Section 52 of the CGST Act (computed via our <a href="/tcs-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">e-commerce TCS calculator</a>) and 0.1% TDS under Section 194-O of the Income Tax Act (calculated via our <a href="/tds-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">Section 194-O TDS calculator</a>) are automatically deducted on the net taxable supply value.
        </li>
      </ul>

